# Vercel deploys the DOCS SITE only — aegrys/web/static/ — and nothing else.
#
# The dashboard's control API (aegrys/web/server.py) must never be deployed. It
# spawns processes, writes to a child process's stdin, and reports local
# filesystem paths, with no authentication of any kind. That is acceptable bound
# to 127.0.0.1 on a machine you own; it is not acceptable on a public URL.
#
# Vercel auto-detects the `app` variable in server.py as a Python serverless
# entrypoint, so excluding every .py file here is what stops that. vercel.json
# pins the output directory as the primary control; this file is the backstop.
#
# NOTE: do NOT add `aegrys/` as a directory exclusion. gitignore syntax cannot
# re-include a path underneath an excluded directory, so that would also drop
# aegrys/web/static — the files we are actually deploying. Excluding `*.py`
# matches at any depth and leaves the static assets intact.

# --- every Python file, at any depth (this is what kills the entrypoint) ---
*.py

# --- directories with nothing the site needs ---
bench/
docs/
exercises/
scripts/
tests/
.cache/
.venv/
dist/
.git/

# --- local-only artefacts ---
*.log
*.jsonl
*.db
*.sqlite
*.wav
*.onnx

# --- repo metadata not needed to serve static files ---
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
.python-version
